From Q9.13.1, the state matrix is, \[A=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; 0\\
1 &amp; -1
\end{array}\right]\] State transition matrix is given by, \[\phi(t)=e^{At}
=
\mathcal{L}^{-1}\left\{
(sI-A)^{-1}
\right\}\] First compute \(sI-A\), \[sI-A=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
s+1 &amp; 0\\
-1 &amp; s+1
\end{array}\right]\] Determinant is, \[|sI-A|
=
(s+1)^2\] Therefore, \[(sI-A)^{-1}
=
\frac{1}{(s+1)^2}
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
s+1 &amp; 0\\
1 &amp; s+1
\end{array}\right]\] \[=
